From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:36:09 -0400
Subject: feat: the address in the sidebar, and essentials per row

GitHub issue 45, its second idea. "Show the address in the sidebar" puts
Back, Forward and Reload on the open sidebar's top row, on the toggle's
line and drawn as the toggle is, and the page's site in a field under
it: a press opens Cmd-L's bar. The window feeds the field and Reload
what it feeds the address row, so the held page and the loading state
carry over. The address row hides while the sidebar is open, under the
rule's exceptions: a localhost page, shift-cmd-D, macOS full screen and
Windows' caption buttons keep it. "Essentials per row" fixes the most
cards a row of the grid holds: Automatic, up to 3 or up to 4. Each has a
Settings row and a command bar row.

Why: GitHub issue 45; the owner said yes on 2026-10-27 and asked on
2026-11-01 for it to be built here.
Removable when: never as a feature; the browser view and grid hunks go
if Chromium's sidebar gains an address of its own or a column count.
